# Known Issues

This file tracks known bugs, limitations, and deferred work items for the project.

## How to Use

- **Before working on a component**: Check this file for known problems
  that may affect your work or that your work could address.
- **When discovering a new issue**: Add an entry with status, date, component,
  problem description, and any known root cause or workaround.
- **When resolving an issue**: Update the status to "Resolved" with the date and
  a brief note on the fix, but keep the entry for historical context.

## Current Open Issues

- **ML Table Detection underperforms heuristic** -- `MLTableDetection/TableDetectorML.py`
  exists and has been trained through five iterations (v2, v4, v5, v5b, v6).
  The best model is still **v4**, which averages mAP@0.5 = 0.47 across 5
  held-out PDFs (best: `Electrical_Takeoff_page7=1.00`; previously-documented
  headline: `generic3=0.66`; worst: `K=0.13`). See the
  "v4 held-out baseline -- DONE 2026-05-07" entry below for the full per-PDF
  table. v4 still trails the heuristic `PanelSearchToolV25` which finds all
  6 panels on generic3. Adding negative examples (v5, v5b) caused regressions;
  the v6 retrain on the expanded 298-image dataset (Phase 2.b on Paperspace,
  2026-05-09) produced an even larger regression -- mAP@0.5 = 0.0337 average,
  a ~14x backslide vs v4.   See the "v6 retrain -- FAIL 2026-05-09" entry below
  for the failure mode (silent model: only 1 prediction at conf >= 0.5 across
  the entire eval set, recall 0.03 vs v4's 0.51). The two cheap recovery
  checks (final checkpoint vs `best/`, confidence sweep down to 0.05) both
  failed on 2026-05-14 -- v6 has effectively collapsed to firing 1 DETR
  object query per page regardless of how many panels are present. Follow-up
  training-time forensics on the same day (`trainer_state.json` +
  `training_args.bin` + a side-by-side hyperparameter diff against v4 +
  a synthetic-positional-bias check) identified the v6 *training recipe*
  (not the architecture and not the dataset) as the cause: v6 froze the
  backbone for the first 9 epochs and then unfroze it under a halved
  peak LR (5e-6 vs v4's 1e-5) that was already 67% decayed by the
  unfreeze step, leaving the backbone effectively untrained. See the
  "v6 root-cause investigation -- DONE 2026-05-14" entry below for the
  full evidence chain. The recommended next step is now a **recipe-fix
  retrain (v7)** with v4's hyperparameters on v6's expanded dataset,
  before any escalation to Phase 3 (RF-DETR). v4 remains the best Table
  Transformer model in the meantime.
  **Root cause identified (2026-05-06)**: dataset size is the primary bottleneck.
  Microsoft Table Transformer maintainers recommend ~1,000 images as the
  fine-tuning floor (per [microsoft/table-transformer Issue #108](https://github.com/microsoft/table-transformer/issues/108));
  the original `annotations_coco.json` had only 28 images with annotations.
  See "Dataset expansion (Phase 1) -- DONE" entry below for the v6 dataset and
  the "Phase 2 audit gaps -- DONE" entry for the training-script changes.
  Evaluation infrastructure already exists at `MLTableDetection/evaluate_model.py`
  (modes: `--data` for COCO mAP, `--images` for inference, `--pdf` for
  box-level ML-vs-heuristic comparison with mAP / precision / recall / mean IoU).

